  "description": "In the ground floor flat we would like to install 1 air-con unit in our living room (the room facing our garden). After consulting with the aircon installation team, the best place to put it would be on the inside of the angled wall. It would mean having a 10-15 cm pipe on the outside of the wall of our extension, facing the freeholders garden and place the outdoor unit on the roof of our extension. I have a picture I would like to attach for reference (hopefully the form will let me add documents later on). The freeholder have given their consent in email given that we have all the necessary approvals in place, and ensuring the unit does not cause nuisance to the first floor flat and that any run off pipe would need to be discharging on to our part of the garden.\n\nThe aircon company is fully REFCOM-certified and complies with all relevant F-Gas regulations and installation best practices. \n\n",
